  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARM: Resilient Voices: Strengthening Public Interest Media for Armenia&#x2019;s 2026 Elections</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will strengthen the sustainability of public interest media, enabling them to produce independent, high-quality content and address funding challenges. By improving financial viability and enhancing editorial standards, the project will empower public with reliable, evidence-based information, particularly important ahead of the 2026 parliamentary elections.

Six media outlets, selected through an open call, will produce high-quality, evidence-based content on democracy, human rights, election issues. This will provide the public with in-depth analysis, bridge gaps, and support informed decision-making in the election context. Outlets will receive tailored mentorship and training from international experts on audience engagement, monetization, and operational efficiency, leading to innovative business models for long-term resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
